export anchor WhiskyBarStyle:
    number: 241
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Whisky bar
    idea:
        A low lit bar of dark leather and walnut with brass rails, where the
        projects stand on a shelf as glasses filled with amber to their
        percent, the figures sit on engraved brass framed plaques and a warm
        amber glow lights the greeting.
    base: dark
    palette:
        leather: #1a110c, the page and the style sheet
        walnut: #2a1a10, the header band, panels and the shelf back
        walnutLight: #352215, plaques, fields and the current nav item
        glow: #3d2716, the brightest point of the amber glow, the lightest surface text sits on
        line: #5a3f27, panel borders and ledger rules
        brass: #d1ad66, rails, frames, the primary button, links, glass outlines and focus
        brassInk: #1d130b, text on brass
        ink: #f2e4cc, text and figures
        muted: #c8b293, meta, labels and axis text
        amber: #f0a24a, the liquid in the glasses and this week bars
        oak: #9a7448, last week bars
        ok: #b6dd8f, On track text and check circle
        risk: #f5cd6a, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #ff9f86, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings and body use Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face,
        Hoefler Text, Georgia, serif, with the greeting 36px, plaque figures
        38px with lining numbers, project names 17px at 600 and body 15px at
        1.55. Labels and meta use engraved caps, Copperplate, Copperplate
        Gothic Light, Engravers MT, serif, 12 to 15px tracked 0.18em.
    layout:
        A walnut header band with faint grain ends in a 3px brass rail. It
        holds the Brightwork name engraved on a small brass plaque, the six
        nav links in engraved caps with Home on a darker inset tile with a
        brass underline, a leather search field, a bell, a brass New project
        button and Mara Okafor. Below, a wide walnut panel carries a soft
        amber glow behind the greeting at left, with the date and a coral line
        reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock, and the four figures at
        right as brass framed plaques with a double bevel border, overdue with
        a coral figure. The projects stand on The shelf, a walnut panel with a
        brass shelf edge, as six tall glasses drawn in brass outline, each
        filled with amber to its percent with the percent above, and under
        each glass the name, category, status with its symbol, tasks and due
        date. Below the shelf two panels sit side by side, the chart as paired
        bars for each weekday with oak last week and glowing amber this week,
        and the ledger of activity with ruled lines and engraved times. Below
        1000px the glasses wrap to three per row and the panels stack, below
        600px the glasses wrap to two per row and plaques go two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 28px panel padding, 20px between glasses, 32px between panels.
    density: Medium. A rich shelf with room around each glass.
    corners: Small. 4px panels, plaques, buttons and fields, glasses with rounded bases.
    borders:
        Brass. A 3px brass rail under the header, double bevelled brass frames
        on plaques, 1px line on panels and ledger rules.
    shadows:
        A warm amber glow behind the greeting and this week bars, and inner
        shadows that make plaques look inset.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.7px stroke in brass. Status uses a check circle, a
        triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
        overdue a clock.
    focus: A 2px brass outline offset 3px with a faint amber glow.
    tone: Warm and a little formal, such as Good morning, Mara, The shelf and The ledger.
